    {
        var result = F(5, 8);

        foreach (var tuple in result)
        {
            Console.WriteLine($"{tuple.Item1}, {tuple.Item2?.Value ?? "N/A"}");
        }
    }

    // Include the helper methods here or place them in a separate class/file
    // You can copy the helper methods into this file or a separate class.
}
```

---

### Notes

- **Tuples with nulls:** C# doesn't have a built-in `null` for generic tuple elements, so we use `int?` (nullable int) for the second item.
